[
  {
    "text": "The classification of translating long-term memory into embodied plans as a subproblem of partial observability and overwritten world states does not imply it is a solved or trivial subproblem.",
    "topic": "subproblem persistency"
  },
  {
    "text": "Persistent implementation difficulties (e.g., memory indexing, grounding, plan coherence) can constitute challenges even when they are nested within a broader category of challenge.",
    "topic": "implementation vs fundamental"
  },
  {
    "text": "The WorldLines paper's framing addresses the dependency structure of challenges, not a claim that the translation process itself lacks independent difficulty.",
    "topic": "framing interpretation"
  },
  {
    "text": "A challenge being a 'subproblem' does not contradict it being 'persistent'; the persistence may stem from the subproblem's own complexity, not from being misclassified.",
    "topic": "logical relation"
  }
]
